      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 8324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-31T13:07:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is quite a problem... here we\u0027re executing a blocking read for up-to 30s for every channel transition (CONNECTING/IDLE/TRANSIENT_FAILURE - flaps included) on the gRPC channel-executor thread. And this is synchronized on the same monitor as the DeviceConnectionManager.closeConnection(). So for 30s the gRPC thread holds this monitor. This will stall every concurrent closeConnection() and every in-flight createMountPoint() rendering the entire southbound connect/disconnect path effectively dead.",
      "revId": "b471a67ec693a5734b2e0f53f0d35da95ffa1323",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a6b8fbd3_c08b3d09",
        "filename": "modules/gnmi-sb/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/gnmi/southbound/device/session/listener/GnmiConnectionStatusListener.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 144,
      "author": {
        "id": 8324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-31T13:07:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here we\u0027re potentially throwing away fully functional and properly mounted connections as FAILED. Let\u0027s say the mountpoint was registered, activeDevices populated, capabilities written and then presence-read throws Execution/TimeoutException. We return the FailedFluentFuture(TimeoutException) to copyDeviceStatusReadyToDatastore() and prepareDeviceConnection() where it reaches Futures.catchingAsync(..., GnmiConnectionStatusException.class, ...). Since TimeoutException does not match that class, it is further propagated to GnmiNodeListener.onFailure. We\u0027re identifying a \"could not tell\" as \"connection broken\" if we do it like this..",
      "revId": "b471a67ec693a5734b2e0f53f0d35da95ffa1323",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a624fb1_afc3097b",
        "filename": "modules/gnmi-sb/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/gnmi/southbound/device/session/listener/GnmiConnectionStatusListener.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 8324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-31T13:07:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will lead to writeStateToDataStore() calling .get() on the failed future - resulting in ExecutedException(InterruptedException). It will get caught by the catch (ExecutionException | TimeoutException) branch and will log \"Unable to write connection state …\" instead of the InterruptedException branch\u0027s \"Interrupted while writing …\".",
      "revId": "b471a67ec693a5734b2e0f53f0d35da95ffa1323",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
